# Rextensions

Chrome MV3 popup extension: manage installed extensions, export/import lists, and cloud backup/restore via Firebase.

## Stack

- Vue 3 + TypeScript + Pinia + Vue Router (hash history for extension pages)
- Vite 7 build → load **`dist/`** in Chrome (not repo root)
- Tailwind 4 + shadcn-vue (Reka UI) under `src/components/ui/`
- Firebase Auth + Firestore (`src/utils/firebase.ts`); **Google-only** sign-in via Chrome Identity (`src/utils/chromeGoogleAuth.ts`)

## Commands

- `npm run build` — production build
- `npm run dev` — `vite build --watch` (reload extension in `chrome://extensions` after rebuild)
- `npm run deploy` — `./deploy.sh` (build + load instructions)

## Key paths

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `public/manifest.json` | MV3 manifest; OAuth client id placeholder `__INJECT_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID__` |
| `popup.html` / `src/popup.ts` | Popup entry |
| `src/background.ts` | Service worker (management message handlers) |
| `src/stores/useExtensionsStore.ts` | Local list, import/export, Firestore backup |
| `src/stores/useAuthStore.ts` | Auth state + `chrome.storage.local` cache |
| `src/views/HomeView.vue` / `AuthView.vue` | Main UI |
| `vite.config.js` | Injects `VITE_CHROME_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` into `dist/manifest.json` on build |

## Env

Copy `.env.example` → `.env`. Set `VITE_CHROME_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` (Chrome extension OAuth client). Never commit `.env`.

## Auto-imports

`unplugin-auto-import` covers `vue` / `pinia` / `vue-router` plus `src/composables/**`, `src/stores/**`, `src/utils/**`. Prefer relying on auto-imports over redundant manual imports for those APIs.
